<title>USA: Trism sees $2.5-$3.5 mln 1st-half charges.</title>
<headline>Trism sees $2.5-$3.5 mln 1st-half charges.</headline>
<dateline>KENNESAW, Ga. 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trism Inc on Wednesday said it expected restructuring charges of $2.5 million to $3.5 million in the first half of 1997.</p>
<p>The charges are related to a plan to consolidate management of four separate business units, a move intended to reduce inefficiency and boost profitability, it said.</p>
<p>Trism -- a trucking company specializing in hauling heavy machinery, equipment, explosives and radioactive materials -- said the four divisions would retain their separate focuses while supporting functions would be combined.</p>
</text>
